/*Q11. An English teacher assigns a task to students: given a string, they need to write the same string such that the first half of the letters are in
lowercase and the second half of the letters are in uppercase.
Write a Java program to implement this string transformation.
Input Format:
• A single line containing the input string.
Output Format:
• Asingle line containing the transformed string, where the first half of the string is in lowercase and the second half of the string is in
uppercase.
• Non-alphabetic characters in the string remain unchanged.
Note:
• For strings with an odd number of characters, the middle character should be included in the second half.
• You can determine the midpoint using integer division.
*/
import java.util.Scanner;
 
public class HalfCase {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        String s = sc.nextLine();
        int mid = s.length() / 2;           // middle char (odd length) goes to second half
        String result = s.substring(0, mid).toLowerCase() + s.substring(mid).toUpperCase();
        System.out.println(result);
        sc.close();
    }
}
